# Neo Scope parameters (docs/specs/machines.md §5). The order is permanent: songs and presets
# store values by position. Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoScope
namespace NeoBuzz.Scope
class NeoScopeMachine
summary Oscilloscope and vectorscope that pass the audio through untouched: the waveform (left, right, mid, side, or left and right overlaid) over a time base synced to the song (1/16 note to 4 bars, aligned to the bar so a loop stands still) or free in time per division with an edge trigger, and a goniometer or polar vectorscope with a correlation meter. Use it to show the user a signal while it plays (a loop's waveform standing still, a synth's cycle, the stereo image); machine_readings gives its peak, RMS, correlation and trigger lock. To look at audio yourself, render and use plot (waveform, goniometer) and analyze.

group Scope
Display   "Display"      0 4    4    enum L R Mid Side L_&_R                         | What the scope draws: the left or right channel, mid (L + R)/2, side (L − R)/2, or left and right overlaid
Sync      "Sync"         0 7    3    enum Free 1/16 1/8 1/4 1/2 1_bar 2_bars 4_bars | The screen's width as a note value of the song's tempo, its sweeps starting on the song's beats and bars (a bar is 4 beats), so a loop stands still; while the song stands still it runs free at the tempo. Free: Time/div and the trigger
Time      "Time/div"     0 1000 394  time 0.0001 0.2                             | With Sync Free: the time per division, 10 across the screen (0.1 ms – 200 ms)
group Trigger
Trigger   "Trigger"      0 2    1    enum Off Rising Falling                     | With Sync Free: each sweep starts where the first trace crosses Level going up (Rising) or down (Falling); with no crossing for two sweeps' time (at least 100 ms) it runs free until one comes. Off: sweeps follow each other
Level     "Level"        0 2000 1000 lin -100 100 % 1                            | The trigger's level, in percent of full scale (0 dBFS)
Holdoff   "Holdoff"      0 1000 0    pow 0 500 2 ms 1                            | After a sweep, the trigger waits this long before it looks for the next crossing (0 – 500 ms)
group View
AutoScale "Auto scale"   0 1    1    switch                                      | On: both displays fit the signal (the scope its sweep's peak, the vectorscope its points). Off: Gain
Gain      "Gain"         0 120  24   db -12 48                                   | With Auto scale Off: the vertical gain of both displays, in 0.5 dB steps (0 dB: full scale fills the screen)
Trail     "Trail"        0 3    1    enum Off Short Medium Long                  | Earlier sweeps stay behind the newest, fading over about 0.15, 0.4 or 1 s
Freeze    "Freeze"       0 1    0    switch                                      | Holds both displays; the readings go on
group Vector
Vector    "Vector"       0 1    0    enum Lissajous Polar                        | Lissajous: the goniometer (mid up, side across, the left channel up-left). Polar: each sample at its angle and level, folded into the upper half (mono straight up, opposed channels along the base)

# What the scope measures (NeoScopeMachine.Readings, machine_readings). Windows end now.
reading peak_dbfs       dBFS  | The highest sample of either channel over the last 3 s
reading rms_db          dB    | The RMS of both channels over the last 3 s, dB (a full-scale sine reads −3 dB, as analyze reads it)
reading correlation     ratio | The correlation of left and right over the last 3 s: 1 mono, 0 unrelated, −1 opposed (the analysis library's)
reading trigger_locked  0/1   | 1 while the sweeps start on the trigger (Sync Free, Trigger Rising or Falling, and the last sweep found its crossing), else 0
